From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:12:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple-g5p: do not refuse system sleep on the render claim

The sleep busy predicate (since "implement bounded retained system
sleep") reads d->accepted as accepted work in flight. It is not: it is
the render claim, set 0 -> 1 by the first accepted job in
g5p_render_device_claim() and never cleared ("one render attachment per
boot: accepted stays held"). Once any client has rendered, which on a
desktop is at boot, every sleep attempt drained for 1 s and refused
"accepted", although no client was in the driver and the firmware was
parked. The deferred-close term hid it until it was dropped.

Accepted jobs not yet signalled are r8_queued (incremented at accept,
decremented at signal), which the predicate already checks. Drop the
claim from the busy states. The R1 quiescent certificate, the rings, the
TA/3D stamps and every other busy state are unchanged.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple-g5p/system-sleep.inc | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple-g5p/system-sleep.inc b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple-g5p/system-sleep.inc
index e93d1b02c..ad782758a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple-g5p/system-sleep.inc
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple-g5p/system-sleep.inc
@@ -18,6 +18,11 @@
  * after an in-boot recovery. With one compositor running, a context that
  * closed earlier stays "previous" for good, so refusing on it refused every
  * sleep.
+ *
+ * Neither is the render claim (d->accepted, g5p_render_device_claim()): it
+ * latches on the first accepted job and holds for the rest of the boot (one
+ * render attachment per boot), so it says nothing about work in flight.
+ * Accepted jobs not yet signalled are r8_queued.
  */
 static const char *g5p_sleep_busy(struct g5p_drm *d, bool *drains)
 {
@@ -42,8 +47,6 @@ static const char *g5p_sleep_busy(struct g5p_drm *d, bool *drains)
 		return "stuck";
 	if (rd->recovering)
 		return "recovering";
-	if (atomic_read(&d->accepted))
-		return "accepted";
 	if (atomic_read(&d->r8_queued))
 		return "r8-queued";
 	if (READ_ONCE(rd->executing))
